SUMMARY:Gibson Park Birding Hike (Jamestown)
DESCRIPTION:From late afternoon to early evening the woods\, lakes\, and wetland of Gibson Park begin to awaken with birdsong. Join NCWF Triad Wild Chapter for a birding hike in Gibson Park as we listen and look for birds! \nThis nearly 2-mile hike will traverse open lake areas\, woods\, and on an observation deck boardwalk for optimal views. At the wetland\, expect to see and hear tons of red-winged blackbirds\, the most prevalent bird in the area. Cardinals\, flycatchers such as eastern phoebes\, Carolina wrens\, herons\, and maybe even the less-common red-headed woodpecker are among the many species active there as well! Beyond birds\, beavers may be active while frogs begin their evening songs. Join us for a birding hike through a variety of habitats! \nREGISTER HERE
URL:https://ncwf.org/event/gibson-park-birding-hike-jamestown/
CATEGORIES:Featured
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://ncwf.org/wp-content/uploads/junebirding.jpg
END:VEVENT
